    {
      "name": "object.union",
      "description": "Creates a new object of the asymmetric union of two objects. For example: `object.union({\"a\": 1, \"b\": 2, \"c\": {\"d\": 3}}, {\"a\": 7, \"c\": {\"d\": 4, \"e\": 5}})` will result in `{\"a\": 7, \"b\": 2, \"c\": {\"d\": 4, \"e\": 5}}`.",
